00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.530
This feels great!

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:38.310
It's like I'm going to melt!

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:44.230
This is shampoo... right?

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:48.830
Whoa, Sensei... yours are huge!{"Woah" to "Whoa" -A0}

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.900
Yeah, I get that a lot.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:54.140
Dammit! She said that so confidently.

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:01.210
D-Don't! Miyamoto-san!

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:06.560
It's not like we're in some lame-ass{gg: steamy} eroge...{Weeaboo editor: okay, I lied about "no translation fixes."}

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.140
Why are we taking a bath together?!

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:11.600
You know why, don't you, Takagi?

00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.040
Yeah, I guess...

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:19.550
But considering our situation,

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:21.610
we shouldn't be letting our guard down like this.

00:03:25.030 --> 00:03:26.570
That sound was more pleasant than I had expected.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:31.080
With an attractive voice like that, any male would...

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:42.460
<i>Argh, she still sounds mature...{Italics added -A0}</i>

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:45.700
Sounds like they're having fun.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.380
Wanna go peek on them, like real men should?

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.370
I don't wanna die yet.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:54.360
We're kinda screwed if this turns out to be empty.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:55.810
There's something in there.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.620
We found the ammo, so there has to be.

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:00.050
Well, either way...

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:01.430
Let's give it a go.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:04.520
One, two, and three!

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.630
That hurt...

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:13.490
Hey, Hirano!

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:20.450
I knew it!

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:24.070
Shizuka-sensei said her friend lives here, right?

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.630
What does her friend do with these?!

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:29.560
What's wrong?

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.370
Someone's probably talking behind my back.

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.100
Who?

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.200
I don't have that many friends,

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:37.450
so it's probably...

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.540
Springfield M1A1 Super Match, eh?

00:04:44.960 --> 00:04:50.520
It's semi-auto. Which is fine, because the M14 series' full-auto is just a waste of bullets anyway.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:50.530
Umm, Hirano?

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:53.150
The magazine holds twenty rounds.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:55.240
This is fucking illegal in Japan!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.330
Hey... Hirano!

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:59.110
Knight's SR-25 Enhanced match rifle!

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.200
Wait, you can't get these in Japan,

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:04.630
so it must be a modified AR-10!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.340
The other one in the locker is a crossbow!

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.670
It's a descendant of one that Robin Hood used!

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.030
A Barnett Wildcat C5!

00:05:12.130 --> 00:05:15.230
It's made in Britain! You can even kill a bear with this thing!

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:18.560
That's an Ithaca M-37 riot shotgun!

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:21.260
It's an awesome gun made by the Americans!

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:23.480
It played a huge role in the Vietnam war!

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:24.660
Cool...

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:31.860
E-Even if it's not loaded, d-don't point it at someone!

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:33.630
The only ones you should be pointing it at are...

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:36.260
<i>Them</i>, huh?{Italics added -A0}

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.320
I hope that's all I'll have to point it at.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:41.820
You know that's not possible.

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.770
It's only gonna get worse.

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:51.060
In a war like this, there's no surrendering or negotiations or shit like that.

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:53.620
Yeah, you're right...

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.720
That's why...

00:05:57.390 --> 00:05:59.360
Another set of big ones over here!

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:02.960
Komuro, give me a hand, will ya?

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:05.110
It's a pain in the ass to load the clips.

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:07.480
Have you done this before with air guns?

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.370
Nah, with real guns.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:12.950
You've held a real one before?!

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.590
When I went to America...

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:21.450
I got trained for a whole month by a
professional instructor from Blackwater.

00:06:22.220 --> 00:06:24.770
He used to be a Delta Force captain!

00:06:25.930 --> 00:06:29.770
You're an expert when it comes to this kind of thing, eh?{removed "only" from b4 "expert" Leaving it sounds like Komuro is insulting him -A0}

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:31.990
I'm so glad that we're on the same side.

00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:38.050
By the way, who the hell is Shizuka-sensei's friend?

00:06:38.400 --> 00:06:40.160
These guns are definitely illegal.

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.780
Technically speaking, it's not illegal if you buy the parts separately.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:48.770
But it's illegal when you assemble it.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:54.000
She mentioned something about her friend being in the Special Assault Team, S.A.T.{"special forces, SAT..." to "Special Assault Team, S.A.T." for clarity -A0}

00:06:54.900 --> 00:06:56.660
Everything's fine if you work for the police, huh?

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.400
Well, we know that this isn't just your average citizen.

00:06:59.960 --> 00:07:04.090
Police officers that aren't married
usually have to live in dormitories.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.290
But if she can afford to rent a place like this...

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.240
Either her parents are rich,

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.610
or the man she's dating is rich,

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.610
or maybe she's involved in some serious shit.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.770
They're being too noisy...

00:07:21.050 --> 00:07:22.150
It's fine.

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:27.050
<i>They</i> react to noise, but the noise is all coming from...{Italics added -A0}

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.740
Get away from anyone dangerous,

00:07:31.970 --> 00:07:34.170
even if they're your family members.

00:07:34.580 --> 00:07:37.590
I won't let anyone who's been attacked or injured through here.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:42.280
A lockdown is in effect here at western Tokonou city.

00:07:42.700 --> 00:07:46.830
However, as this pandemic spreads throughout the world,

00:07:46.830 --> 00:07:51.770
one in ten people are doubting the effectiveness of these lockdowns.

00:07:52.820 --> 00:08:01.180
Those of us that were left behind due to lack of transportation to our offshore facility

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:04.930
will continue to report on the current situation in Tokonou city through satellite communications.

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.390
What do you mean when you tell us to, "Just do whatever"?!{parentheses added - and J for j -A0}

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.300
What about the backup from the prefectural headquarters?

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.720
Communications were cut off?!

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:13.710
Dammit!

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:18.090
Sir, at this rate, the barricade isn't going to hold.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.170
Well, that's a given.

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:24.890
We don't have enough people, and some of the men here are normally office workers.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:26.770
But!

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:30.580
We've received an order from above.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.270
We're permitted to do anything to maintain order.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:36.700
It seems that they're not doing well over there either.

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.050
The last order they received from headquarters was

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:43.650
to do whatever they could.

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:45.740
Then give us an order!

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:48.730
Even if there're unharmed citizens over there... {"there's" to "there're" -A0}

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.910
...we're going to have to sacrifice them for the greater good.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.750
Our job is supposed to be protecting the citizens.

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:00.450
Dammit!

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:05.440
It hasn't even been two days since this all began!

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:24.790
What the hell is this?

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.330
It's like a horror movie.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:32.810
I remember a scene like this in Apocalypse Now.

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:35.020
What's that?

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:37.320
What's up?

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.370
Turn on the TV.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:45.240
This abuse of power by the police is unforgivable!

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:46.450
Unforgivable!

00:09:46.800 --> 00:09:54.300
We believe that this killer pandemic... is caused by biological weapons...{Ellipses added to mimic the cadence -A0}

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:57.230
developed by our government... and foreign nations!{Ellipses added to mimic the cadence -A0}

00:09:54.530 --> 00:10:02.670
Right now, we're live at a demonstration by those that are against this lockdown.

00:09:58.750 --> 00:10:02.660
We condemn those that caused this killer pandemic!

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.710
Killer pandemic...

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:05.890
The nature of this group is unknown.

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:06.500
I guess they're talking about the living dead.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.440
According to these handouts from the group,

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:13.090
they believe that this was caused by the leak of a biological weapon

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:19.250
developed by the Japanese and American governments.

00:10:19.250 --> 00:10:20.480
Are you serious?!

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.310
Biological weapon?! Seriously?!

00:10:22.630 --> 00:10:27.580
There's no way science can explain how corpses are able to move and attack people.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:30.790
Well, that would be the usual back story if we were in a movie or a game.

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:31.930
Or maybe— {"..." to "—" -A0}

00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:39.930
I didn't give you permission to fire!{"permit you" to "give you permission" for flow -A0}

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:50.960
Stop it!

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.230
Don't shoot!

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.310
This child and I are still alive!

00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:58.060
We're still alive!

00:10:59.080 --> 00:10:59.830
I-I beg you...

00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:05.310
Please... Please save my child!

00:11:48.020 --> 00:11:53.410
The despicable police have... finally resorted to...{Ellipses added to mimic the cadence -A0}

00:11:53.630 --> 00:11:58.440
indiscriminately using violence... against the citizens!{Ellipses added to mimic the cadence -A0}

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:04.600
This abuse of power by the police is... unforgivable!{Ellipses added to mimic the cadence -A0}

00:12:03.320 --> 00:12:05.850
Hey, get that person on film.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.590
Unforgivable!

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.290
Unforgivable!

00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:14.550
Stand down immediately.

00:12:15.690 --> 00:12:17.540
It's dangerous for you guys to be here too.

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:23.510
Screw you! You're just trying to cover up the conspiracy framed by our government.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:24.680
I'll repeat myself one last time.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:26.740
Disband immediately.

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:29.440
I refuse. Go away!

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:33.980
Go away! Go away! Go away!{switched to Top-A0}

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:39.500
We've been ordered to take any measure necessary to maintain order.{switched to Default -A0}

00:12:40.360 --> 00:12:42.300
It's not exactly legal, but...

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.150
The order is absolute.

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:47.960
Huh?

00:12:57.820 --> 00:12:59.430
This is insane...

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:01.020
This is bad.

00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:07.200
I think we better get moving.

00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:11.780
That's a bad idea. We won't be able to see as well in the dark.

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:20.670
Komuro-kun~!

00:13:27.160 --> 00:13:28.230
Sorry!

00:13:29.190 --> 00:13:31.520
And Sensei, are you...

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:34.700
It's fine, isn't it?

00:13:34.720 --> 00:13:36.610
Just for a little bit.

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:43.650
Kouta-chan! {W.E.: tbh, this is about the only scene in the first 6 eps where the presence or absence of honorifics really "matters"}

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:44.620
"-chan"?

00:13:44.910 --> 00:13:46.050
Umm, uhh...

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:52.100
You've been a good boy, so here's your reward.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.610
We shouldn't be loud.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:07.990
Please go back downstairs.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:13.450
No way, I'm scared when it's too quiet.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:16.580
I wanna stay here forever...

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:21.390
Shizuka-sensei?

00:14:23.790 --> 00:14:26.540
I just wanna stay like this.

00:14:27.450 --> 00:14:28.210
What?

00:14:27.740 --> 00:14:29.340
Hirano, be on the lookout.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:31.560
Huh... Oh.

00:14:35.110 --> 00:14:36.710
Hang on.

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:42.280
You're touching my ass!

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:45.110
Komuro-kun, you perv.

00:14:45.710 --> 00:14:47.380
That's naughty.

00:14:51.450 --> 00:14:54.910
I'd be really happy if I did that intentionally.

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:59.480
You'd be happy about what?

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:01.090
Ah, I mean...

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:03.700
N-Nothing...

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.330
I was just, uhh...

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:11.700
Ah, there's three Takashi's! {W.E.: Apparently minors aren't allowed to actually *drink* alcohol under Japanese TV restrictions, but being mysteriously drunk is A-Okay!}

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.010
Huh?

